# Stafford needs no environment variables to build or run. There are no secrets
# to set here: the one token Stafford uses lives at ~/.agent-dashboard/token on
# the machine, never in the repo or in an env file.
#
# This file exists so the pattern is in place if a real setting is ever needed:
# copy it to .env (which is gitignored) and set values there. Nothing reads .env
# today.
#
# For reference, the app does read a few optional variables from the process
# environment. None are required and none are secrets. They are internal knobs
# for development and the smoke and screenshot harness, not things a normal run
# sets:
#
#   STAFFORD_APP_ID           run under a distinct app id and data dir, so a
#                             packaged verification can coexist with a live
#                             Stafford instead of colliding on the fixed pipe
#   STAFFORD_ENABLE_LOGIN_ITEM opt a dev run into registering the login item
#   STAFFORD_SMOKE            smoke and screenshot harness toggles, plus the
#   STAFFORD_TASK_SMOKE       matching _CWD, _EFFECT, and _LOG variants used by
#   STAFFORD_TASK_UI_SMOKE    the harness scripts
#   STAFFORD_DELIVERY_SMOKE
